package entity

// pettaunthate.go — an enchanter's pet's taunt gives 70% of the threat it gave (the GM Jibwiz's
// petition 1928, 2026-11-13: "Reduce the agro generated by enchanters Grand animation and other
// enchanter pet line pets via their taunt by 30%").
//
// A pet's taunt (pet.go petTauntLocked: the Grand Animation and any enchanter's pet with no template
// row; pettemplate.go petTemplateTauntLocked: the "pet animation" template's animations and golems,
// Gymon's Animation, the Earthen and Ferrous Golems) raises the pet's threat on its target to one above
// the top and lands a hit, whose damage is hate as any hit's. For a pet an enchanter summoned
// (petState.enchanter, a merc enchanter's too), all the threat the taunt added, the raise and its
// hit's, is cut to enchanterPetTauntHatePct of it, and the creature chooses its enemy again from its
// list (pickEnemyLocked): the pet no longer always lands on top, it takes the creature only when its
// threat after the taunt is the highest. A charmed creature's and a merc's own are as they were; a
// training dummy's hate is its own (dummy.go) and a Metal Moogie keeps to his challenger, so neither is
// cut.
//
// The magician's earth pets (the "pet earth" template's: the elementaling, elementalkin and elemental
// lines and the level 60 Summon Badi, petState.earth) are cut the same way to earthPetTauntHatePct
// (the GM Jibrish's petition 5034, 2026-11-14: "Mage earth pets taunt a bit too hard, lower their
// threat/aggro generated by their taunts by 5% across the board"): the raise to the top and its margin
// (pettauntmargin.go) and the taunt's hit, 95% of what they added.
const (
	enchanterPetTauntHatePct = 70
	earthPetTauntHatePct     = 95
	// magicianEarthTemplate is the pettemplate row the magician's earth pets fight by.
	magicianEarthTemplate = "pet earth"
)

// petTauntHatePct is the part of the threat a pet's taunt adds that it keeps (the file's doc): 100
// for a pet whose taunt is not cut.
func petTauntHatePct(ps *petState) int {
	switch {
	case ps.enchanter:
		return enchanterPetTauntHatePct
	case ps.earth:
		return earthPetTauntHatePct
	}
	return 100
}

// petTauntHateCutLocked takes the pet's threat on t before its taunt and returns what cuts the threat
// the taunt added (the file's doc), to run after it (a defer). Nothing for a pet neither an
// enchanter's nor a magician's earth pet, a dummy or a Metal Moogie's duel. Must be called with the
// lock held.
func (w *World) petTauntHateCutLocked(ps *petState, t *NPC) func() {
	pct := petTauntHatePct(ps)
	if pct >= 100 || ps.npc.Charm != nil || t.Dummy != NotDummy || t.challenge != nil {
		return func() {}
	}
	id := ps.npc.ServerID
	before := t.Threats[id]
	return func() {
		after, ok := t.Threats[id]
		if t.Dead || !ok || after <= before {
			return
		}
		t.Threats[id] = before + pctOf(after-before, pct)
		if e := w.pickEnemyLocked(t); e != 0 {
			t.CurrentEnemy = e
		}
	}
}
